    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370-a1">

                <pb facs="0413" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg315"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Delcassé to Mr.
                            Vignaud.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Charge d’affaires</hi>: You have been kind enough
                    to communicate to me, under date of yesterday, the contents of a telegram which
                    you have received from the Federal secretary of state for foreign affairs, which
                    treats of an exchange of communications <pb facs="0414" n="316" xml:id="pg316"/>
                    between your Government and the viceroy of the two Kuang, relative to the
                    situation of the foreign representatives at Pekin.</p>
                <p>In thanking you for having transmitted to me this document, I am pleased to
                    testify to the commonality of views existing between the Government of the
                    United States and that of the French Republic.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Chargé d’Affaires, the assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Delcassé</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
